                <pb facs="0984" n="864" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg864"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111—Lundeen, Anton: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-17T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 17—10:43
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>420. American citizen, Anton Lundeen of Newman Grove, Nebraska, member of
                    Augustana Synod Mission, reported captured by [brigands] at Juchow, Honan,
                    October 13, following looting of mission station there. Other American missions
                    reported safe. Representations have been made to the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs by the Legation and to provisional [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >provincial?</hi>] authorities Honan and Hupeh by the consul general,
                    Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
